# wiki-events: tick
# wiki-setup: yes
# wiki-settings: yes
# wiki-detect: .github/workflows+remote:github
"""wiki github: an llm-wiki extension. Standard library only.

For agents that have no CI watching of their own. It asks GitHub, through the gh program, which
workflow runs are failing in a clone's repository, and why: the failing job and step, the first
line that looks like the error, and a short excerpt of the failing step's log, kept on this
machine. With a folder watched, the tick event leaves a line for the next session on that branch
when a run starts failing, and can save a note in the wiki when the failure is fixed.

It READS GitHub: gh run list, gh run view, gh pr list, gh repo view, gh auth status, and, before a fix, gh api
repos/<owner>/<repo>/actions/runs/<id>. It writes
there only when a person has turned fixing on for a clone, at a terminal (wiki github fix on):
then, for a run that starts failing on a pull request's branch you opened or on the default
branch, it starts your agent on a fresh worktree and, after its own checks, pushes ONE commit to
that pull request's branch, or pushes a new branch and opens a pull request (gh pr create). The
change is frozen into git objects, checked there and committed from them, with none of the
repository's hooks run, and pushed by commit id to the address the clone's origin had when the run
failed. It never force-pushes, never pushes to the default branch, never reruns or cancels a run,
never merges, and never reads, asks for, prints or stores a token: gh holds the sign-in.
"""
